From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: ASoC: h713: add the codec capture path

Playback on this codec is finished and correct; capture does not exist. The
card exposes only pcmC0D0p, because the DT declares a tx DMA and nothing else
and the H713 component has no ADC widgets to power.

Worth stating why this is not a small change: mainline's H616 support, which
the H713 variant is built on, has **no capture path at all** -- zero ADC
widgets, zero ADC routes, and a DT node with only a tx DMA. There is no
upstream reference for this codec generation, so the register map comes from
the vendor driver, corroborated against the stock DTB wherever it can be:

  SUNXI_ADC_FIFOC   0x030     ADC FIFO control
  SUNXI_ADC_RXDATA  0x040     DMA source; stock's dummy_cpudai independently
                              carries adc_txdata = <0x2030040>
  SUNXI_ADCL/R_REG  0x300/4   per-channel analog control, enable at bit 19,
                              global enable at bit 31
  dmas                        stock: <&dma 7>, <&dma 7> / "tx", "rx" -- capture
                              shares the playback channel

The 0xFF mixer field at the bottom of ADCL/ADCR is left alone at its reset
value of 0x55, which is also the value the vendor driver writes. No source
identified which input that selects, so guessing at it would only add an
unfalsifiable variable to the first measurement.

The DAI already declares a "Codec Capture" stream, so nothing is needed there.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH, and the reason the input widget is named "Mic"
provisionally: nobody has established that an analog input is populated on this
board. The evidence is suggestive but not conclusive -- stock sets
capture_cma = <0x100> and lists a codec_adc clock, and the SoC has a MICBIAS
register at 0x318 reading 0x40003030 -- but a SoC having a mic bias generator
says nothing about what is soldered to it. The same trap ate several hours on
the playback side, where every control moved the right register bits and
nothing was audible because the speaker was on a different amplifier.

So this is judged on one thing only: whether pcmC0D0c appears and a recording
contains something other than a flat line. If it captures silence, the next
question is the analog input, not the digital path.

RESULT SO FAR: the component is correct, the PCM is not. After booting this,
the card still reports

  00-00: CDC PCM Codec-0 : CDC PCM Codec-0 : playback 1

with no capture substream, while ASoC debugfs shows every new widget alive:

  ADC Enable  Codec Capture  Left ADC  Right ADC  Mic  ...

Verified in the built artifact rather than assumed, and each of these was
checked individually, so none of them is the remaining cause:

  - dai_link->playback_only is false in the H713 card (the H616 inheritance
    that first suppressed it);
  - quirks->playback_only is unset, so probe configures capture_dma_data;
  - reg_adc_fifoc and reg_adc_rxdata are set in the quirks;
  - sun4i_codec_dai declares a "Codec Capture" stream, and dummy_cpu_dai
    declares a capture stream too, so both ends of the link support it;
  - sun4i_codec_dai_probe passes capture_dma_data to
    snd_soc_dai_init_dma_data;
  - the live DT carries dma-names "tx" "rx" with two dma cells;
  - the codec probes with no error and no DMA complaint in dmesg.

So the remaining suspect is the generic dmaengine PCM platform: whether it
actually obtained an "rx" channel. Mainline sunxi codecs that do capture use
the same pattern this DT now has -- one channel listed twice, e.g. A100's
dmas = <&dma 43>, <&dma 43> with dma-names "rx", "tx" -- with the names in the
opposite order to ours, which should not matter to a by-name lookup but has not
been tested.

Nothing here has been judged by ear or by recording yet, and the physical
question below is still completely open.

OUT OF SERIES until it captures.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
@@ -248,6 +248,23 @@
  * fields in this undocumented register.
  */
 #define SUN50I_H713_HP_REG			(0x324)
+/*
+ * The ADC side of the H713 codec. Mainline's H616 support -- which this variant
+ * is built on -- has no capture path at all: no ADC widgets, no ADC routes, and
+ * a DT node with only a tx DMA. So these come from the vendor register map
+ * rather than from an upstream reference.
+ *
+ * Independently corroborated by the stock DTB, which is the authority here:
+ * its dummy_cpudai node carries adc_txdata = <0x2030040>, matching RXDATA
+ * below, and dmas = <&dma 7>, <&dma 7> with dma-names "tx", "rx" -- capture
+ * shares the playback DMA channel.
+ */
+#define SUN50I_H713_ADC_FIFOC			(0x030)
+#define SUN50I_H713_ADC_RXDATA			(0x040)
+#define SUN50I_H713_ADCL_REG			(0x300)
+#define SUN50I_H713_ADCR_REG			(0x304)
+#define SUN50I_H713_ADCX_EN			(19)
+#define SUN50I_H713_ADCX_GLOBAL_EN		(31)
 #define SUN50I_H713_HP_AMP_EN			(15)
 #define SUN50I_H713_HP_AMP_EN_MASK		BIT(SUN50I_H713_HP_AMP_EN)
 #define SUN50I_H616_DAC_LEN			(15)
@@ -2044,6 +2061,20 @@
 			    sun50i_h713_codec_hp_amp_event,
 			    SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMD),
 
+	/*
+	 * Capture. Each channel has its own analog control register with an
+	 * enable at bit 19 and a global enable at bit 31; the 0xFF mixer field
+	 * below them is left at the vendor's reset value of 0x55, because no
+	 * source has yet identified which input it selects.
+	 */
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_ADC("Left ADC", "Codec Capture",
+			 SUN50I_H713_ADCL_REG, SUN50I_H713_ADCX_EN, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_ADC("Right ADC", "Codec Capture",
+			 SUN50I_H713_ADCR_REG, SUN50I_H713_ADCX_EN, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("ADC Enable", SUN50I_H713_ADCL_REG,
+			    SUN50I_H713_ADCX_GLOBAL_EN, 0, NULL, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_INPUT("Mic"),
+
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT("LINEOUT"),
 };
 
@@ -2339,6 +2370,12 @@
 	{ "Line Out Source Playback Route", "Mono Differential", "Right DAC" },
 	{ "LINEOUT", NULL, "Line Out Source Playback Route" },
 	{ "LINEOUT", NULL, "HP Amp" },
+
+	/* Capture routes */
+	{ "Left ADC", NULL, "ADC Enable" },
+	{ "Right ADC", NULL, "ADC Enable" },
+	{ "Left ADC", NULL, "Mic" },
+	{ "Right ADC", NULL, "Mic" },
 };
 
 static struct snd_soc_card *sun50i_h713_codec_create_card(struct device *dev)
@@ -2354,7 +2391,13 @@
 	if (!card->dai_link)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 
-	card->dai_link->playback_only = true;
+	/*
+	 * H616 sets playback_only here because it has no capture path. This
+	 * variant does, so the link must allow both -- otherwise ASoC drops
+	 * the capture substream and the card exposes pcmC0D0p alone, no
+	 * matter what the DT and the widgets say.
+	 */
+	card->dai_link->playback_only = false;
 	card->dai_link->capture_only = false;
 
 	card->dev		= dev;
@@ -2392,6 +2435,8 @@
 	.create_card	= sun50i_h713_codec_create_card,
 	.reg_dac_fifoc	= REG_FIELD(SUN50I_H616_CODEC_DAC_FIFOC, 0, 31),
 	.reg_dac_txdata	= SUN8I_H3_CODEC_DAC_TXDATA,
+	.reg_adc_fifoc	= REG_FIELD(SUN50I_H713_ADC_FIFOC, 0, 31),
+	.reg_adc_rxdata	= SUN50I_H713_ADC_RXDATA,
 	.has_reset	= true,
 	.dma_max_burst	= SUN4I_DMA_MAX_BURST,
 	.mod_freq_mult	= 2,
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -774,8 +774,13 @@
 				 <&ccu CLK_AUDIO_CODEC_DAC>;
 			clock-names = "apb", "codec";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_AUDIO_CODEC>;
-			dmas = <&dma 7>;
-			dma-names = "tx";
+			/*
+			 * Capture shares the playback DMA channel. Taken from
+			 * the stock DTB's dummy_cpudai, which has
+			 * dmas = <&dma 7>, <&dma 7> and dma-names "tx", "rx".
+			 */
+			dmas = <&dma 7>, <&dma 7>;
+			dma-names = "tx", "rx";
 			/* PL2 on r_pio, NOT PB2 on the main pio. Active high. */
 			allwinner,pa-gpios = <&r_pio 0 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 			/*
